text:
alex: Quick sync 1: final prelaunch SEO/redirect pass for the webinar landing. Need tech checks before paid traffic. Main risk: client-side redirects breaking organic benchmarks.

jess: Noted. Can we disable JS redirects for bots until launch?

sam: Yes. Also add canonical + sitemap priority and Event JSON-LD. I'll draft schema.

alex: Eng asks: (a) X-Robots-Tag: noindex on experimental variants until go-live, (b) avoid client-side path-rewriting 302s  prefer server-side with Vary or server rewrite, (c) add a toggle to suppress redirects for QA.

marco: I can add safe nginx toggle. Example:
```
if ($http_user_agent ~* "Googlebot|Bingbot") {
  add_header X-Robots-Tag "index, follow";
} else {
  return 302 /variant/$arg_variant;
}
```

jess: SEO tasks: Event schema, consistent anchor text "Redwood Inference webinar" from Resources -> landing, and patch top linking pages.

sam: I'll provide JSON-LD (startDate, endDate, location: Online, speakable) and run Screaming Frog anchor export. CSV by EOD.

alex: Redirect mapping: whitelist legacy /webinar-old links. We have incoming links; seo-bot recommends 301 for high-authority referrers and 302 for experiments.

seo-bot: crawl-alert: 3 high-authority inbound links to /webinar-old. Recommend 301 -> /webinar and set canonical accordingly.

marco: Will implement 301 for those hostnames, keep 302 for A/B variants. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/web/compare/webinar-redirect-safety

jess: Form routing: preserve UTM+referrer through redirect chain. Server-side append before redirect.

sam: I'll add Playwright test: simulate redirect, submit form, assert CRM payload contains utm_source.

alex: Owners: alex (product), marco (eng), sam (SEO/analytics). Follow-ups: ScreamingFrog CSV, PR link, final redirect mapping before flip. :white_check_mark:
